tests {
  // ULIP wraps every result in {"response":[...],"error":"false","code":"200","message":"..."},
  // with string-typed error/code, so check the envelope as well as the HTTP status.
  test("envelope error is false and code is 200", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.error, JSON.stringify(body)).to.equal("false");
    expect(body.code, JSON.stringify(body)).to.equal("200");
  });
}

docs {
  # ULIP (Unified Logistics Interface Platform)

  Direct, **read-only** calls to ULIP (not a Vahn service), through the same relay that plutus-java's
  `ULIPClient` uses (`ulip.endpoint` in plutus-java `config.yml`). It covers every ULIP API plutus-java
  calls, plus `SARATHI/01` for driver/DL details (which plutus-api does not expose yet):

  | Folder | API | Input |
  |---|---|---|
  | sarathi | SARATHI/01 driving licence | DL number + DOB |
  | fastag | FASTAG/01 transactions, FASTAG/02 vehicle details | vehicle number |
  | vahan | VAHAN/04 RC details | vehicle number |
  | tgvahan | TGVAHAN/01 Telangana RC details (XML in JSON) | vehicle number |
  | echallan | ECHALLAN/01 e-challans | vehicle number |
  | ewaybill | EWAYBILL/01 e-way bill | e-way bill number |
  | toll | TOLL/01 toll plaza master | `ulipStateName` |
  | bpcl / iocl | BPCL/02, IOCL/02 fuel prices | `ulipBpclStateCode` / `ulipIoclStateCode` |

  ## Credentials and inputs

  Read from `bruno/collections/ulip/.env` (gitignored). Create it locally:

  ```
  ULIP_USERNAME=<ulip username>
  ULIP_PASSWORD=<ulip password>
  ULIP_DL_NUMBER=<driving licence number, e.g. MH1220190012345>
  ULIP_DOB=<licence holder's date of birth, yyyy-MM-dd>
  ULIP_VEHICLE_NUMBER=<registration number, e.g. MH12AB1234>
  ULIP_EWB_NUMBER=<12-digit e-way bill number>
  ULIP_BPCL_REFERENCE_NO=<plutus-java ulip.bpclReferenceNo>
  ULIP_IOCL_REFERENCE_NO=<plutus-java ulip.ioclReferenceNo>
  ```

  DL, DOB, vehicle and e-way bill numbers are customer data, so they live in `.env` rather than the
  env file. State inputs are plain vars in `environments/staging.bru`.

  ## Token

  `auth/login` stores the token with `bru.setVar` (a runtime var), so it is **never written to the env
  file**. Run it before any other request; the CLI runs the whole collection:

  ```bash
  npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/collections/ulip --env staging
  ```

  Every call counts against the account's ULIP quota, which plutus-java's schedulers share.
}
